{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Vāraṇa","html":"<article id='thag3.7'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 3.7 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 3.7 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tikanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Threes </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Paṭhamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter One </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Vāraṇattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Vāraṇa </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yodha koci manussesu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Anyone among men </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>parapāṇāni hiṁsati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who harms other creatures: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Asmā lokā paramhā ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that person will fall </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ubhayā dhaṁsate naro. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>both from this world and the next. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo ca mettena cittena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>But someone with a mind of love, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sabbapāṇānukampati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>sympathetic for all creatures: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bahuñhi so pasavati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a person like that </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>puññaṁ tādisako naro. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>brims with much merit. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Subhāsitassa sikkhetha, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You should all train <j>to learn well-spoken words, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>samaṇūpāsanassa ca; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>to attend closely to ascetics, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ekāsanassa ca raho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>to sit alone in hidden places, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>cittavūpasamassa cā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and to settle the mind. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Vāraṇo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
